  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Calcination is a process in which ore is heated in the absence of air or air might be supplied in a limited quantity.&nbsp;</p><p>Roasting involves the heating of ore lower than its melting point in the presence of air or oxygen.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>PbS</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mover><mo>&#8594;</mo><mo>&#8710;</mo></mover><mn>2</mn><mi>PbO</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>SO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math></p><p>The above reaction is an example of roasting. Rest all the reactions are heated in the absence of oxygen.</p>",
